{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/navbar_guest_card

    The "New here?" card at the top of the mobile primary drawer, for the visitors the navbar's
    actions are drawn for (theme_dimensions/navbar_guest). Below the md breakpoint the navbar keeps
    only "Log in", so this card is where "Create account" and, for the guest account, core's
    "You are currently using guest access" are found. It is included by this theme's override of
    theme_boost/primary-drawer-mobile from the layout context key dimensionsguest, which the theme's
    core renderer writes from theme_dimensions\local\guestnav::context().

    The drawer is not inside the .navbar, so the buttons are Bootstrap's own and read the page's
    colours.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a Mustache
    comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * loginurl - Core's login page, plain
    * hassignup - Whether the site takes sign-ups (core's signup_is_enabled())
    * signupurl - Core's sign-up page, plain; empty without sign-ups
    * isguest - Whether the session is the guest account's

    Example context (json):
    {
        "loginurl": "https://example.com/login/index.php",
        "hassignup": true,
        "signupurl": "https://example.com/login/signup.php",
        "isguest": true
    }
}}
<div class="dimensions-guestcard" data-region="dimensions-guestcard">
    <p class="dimensions-guestcard-title">{{#str}} guestnav_card_title, theme_dimensions {{/str}}</p>
    <p class="dimensions-guestcard-text">{{#str}} guestnav_card_text, theme_dimensions {{/str}}</p>
    <div class="dimensions-guestcard-actions">
        {{#hassignup}}
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{signupurl}}">{{#str}} guestnav_signup, theme_dimensions {{/str}}</a>
        {{/hassignup}}
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="{{loginurl}}">{{#str}} login, core {{/str}}</a>
    </div>
    {{#isguest}}
    <p class="dimensions-guestcard-note">{{#str}} loggedinasguest, core {{/str}}</p>
    {{/isguest}}
</div>
